h 44 (coprime). From 44 reach 11, etc.\n# Let's just find, for each target, a predecessor chain, and assemble.\n# Since union=210, pick start=1, then greedily pick next unvisited remainder reachable\n# in finite steps from current (following the reachable-set closure). \n# Actually simplest rigorous construction:\n\n# Build a DAG on remainders: edge r->s if s in R(r) (one step). Find longest path / \n# a path (walk) covering all nodes using the fact graph is strongly connected enough.\n# We'll do a DFS that allows revisiting to guarantee coverage, ending at 0.\n# Use the CORRECT adj each time (recompute inline to avoid stale issues).\n\ndef build_walk():\n    visited = set()\n    walk = []\n    # DFS but allow revisits to ensure coverage; track walk.\n    def dfs(u):\n        visited.add(u)\n        walk.append(u)\n        for v in sorted(adj[u]):\n            if v not in visited:\n                dfs(v)\n    dfs(1)\n    return walk\n\nwalk = build_walk()\nprint(\"walk covers all 210:\", set(walk) == set(range(N)), \"len:\", len(walk))\nprint(\"0 is last (sink):\", walk[-1] == 0, \"0 index:\", walk.index(0))\n# Now, is the walk valid (each edge in adj)?\nvalid = all(walk[i+1] in adj[walk[i]] for i in range(len(walk)-1))\nprint(\"walk edges valid:\", valid)"}) - MainThread
