ultiple exists (so we never get stuck), and we can route to visit\n#    all 210 (e.g., from 1 reach 44, from 44 reach 11, from 11 reach coprimes,\n#    from 140 reach 70,140,0; from 70 reach 0; etc.). A valid prefix visiting all\n#    210 then repeating 0 gives an infinite sequence with 210 distinct terms.\nprint(\"\\nUnion of all reachable sets = 210. 0 reachable from all nonzero:\", all(0 in reach[r] for r in range(1,N)))"}) - MainThread
