2026-01-01 00:00:00,000[utu.hooks.base_hooks] - DEBUG - base_hooks.py:41 - [toolcall-call_094d793b652d4c3f868ce6d1] execute_python_code({"code": "import sympy as sp\n\n# Foot of perpendicular from point P=(px,py) to line through A=(ax,ay), B=(bx,by)\n# Standard formula\npx,py,ax,ay,bx,by = sp.symbols('px py ax ay bx by', real=True)\nt = ((px-ax)*(bx-ax) + (py-ay)*(by-ay))/((bx-ax)**2 + (by-ay)**2)\nXf = ax + t*(bx-ax)\nYf = ay + t*(by-ay)\nprint(\"Foot X =\", sp.simplify(Xf), \" Y =\", sp.simplify(Yf))\n\n# For A=(0,0), B=(10,0), C=(0,10):\nax,ay,bx,by = 0,0,10,0\nt = ((px-ax)*(bx-ax)+(py-ay)*(by-ay))/((bx-ax)**2+(by-ay)**2)\nXf = ax + t*(bx-ax)\nYf = ay + t*(by-ay)\nprint(\"Xf =\", sp.simplify(Xf), \" Yf =\", sp.simplify(Yf))\n\n# For D=(48√2, 0):\nDx,Dy = 48*sp.sqrt(2), 0\nt = ((Dx-ax)*(bx-ax)+(Dy-ay)*(by-ay))/((bx-ax)**2+(by-ay)**2)\nXfD = ax + t*(bx-ax); YfD = ay + t*(by-ay)\nprint(\"\\nX foot of D=(48√2,0): XfD =\", sp.simplify(XfD), \" YfD =\", sp.simplify(YfD))\n\n# For E=(0, 52√2):\nEx,Ey = 0, 52*sp.sqrt(2)\nt = ((Ex-ax)*(bx-ax)+(Ey-ay)*(by-ay))/((bx-ax)**2+(by-ay)**2)\nXfE = ax + t*(bx-ax); YfE = ay + t*(by-ay)\nprint(\"Y foot of E=(0,52√2): XfE =\", sp.simplify(XfE), \" YfE =\", sp.simplify(YfE))\n\n# Now compute XY\nXY = sp.sqrt(sp.simplify((XfD-XfE)**2 + (YfD-YfE)**2))\nprint(\"\\nXY =\", XY, \"=\", float(XY))", "name": "derive_foot"}) - MainThread
