ce from B:\", np.linalg.norm(Y-B))\nprint(\"Y distance from C:\", np.linalg.norm(Y-C))\n\n# Hmm, the issue: is X really at distance 96 from B?\n# Let me check: AD = 48√2, angle B = 45°\n# BX should be AD*cos(45°) = 48√2 * (√2/2) = 48\n\n# But the geometric gave X at distance 4 from B, not 48!\n# Let me recheck...\n\n# Wait, I think I mislabeled. Let me recompute BX manually.\n# D = (48√2, 0), B = (52√2, 0), C = (0, 52√2)\n# Line BC: from B(52√2,0) to C(0,52√2)\n# Direction: C - B = (-52√2, 52√2)\n# Foot of perp from D:\n# t = (D-B)·(C-B)/|C-B|²\nD_B = D - B\nC_B = C - B\nt = np.dot(D_B, C_B)/np.dot(C_B, C_B)\nprint(\"\\nt for X =\", t)\nX_calc = B + t*C_B\nprint(\"X_calc =\", X_calc)\nprint(\"BX =\", np.linalg.norm(X_calc - B))"}) - MainThread
