 made an error?\n# No - M=2 > m=1 always accelerates toward pulley.\n#\n# Let me reconsider: maybe the answer is just ~62, and I should trust the physics.\n# But let me check the 'nice' target more carefully by trying different g and d.\nprint()\n# Check: does any reasonable config give exactly 100t=10?\n# 100t=10 => t=0.1 => a=2d/t^2=200 m/s^2. \n# Max possible a (M>>m, no friction): a ~ g*cos(theta) ~ 9.8*0.985 = 9.65.\n# So a=200 is physically impossible. 100t=10 is IMPOSSIBLE for this system.\nprint(\"Maximum possible acceleration ~ g*cos(theta) =\", g*c, \"m/s^2\")\nprint(\"So 100t=10 (needs a=200) is physically IMPOSSIBLE.\")\nprint(\"The physically correct answer is 100t ≈ 62.\")"}) - MainThread
